WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.649
What did you learn about the nature of politics?

00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:10.960
And did this made you into a more optimistic
or more pessimistic human being?

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.480
What politics did teach me is that nothing
is impossible.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.060
I grew up in the eastern part of the country,
border of Mozambique.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.340
When the war of liberation started I was a
small boy but I did see the war.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.980
At that time, it was unthinkable that the
guerrillas could defeat this monolithic army,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:38.640
of people who had helicopters, cars, big cars,
big guns.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.160
But I lived to see the system collapse.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.830
I lived to see the people awakening from a position of disadvantage win.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:58.670
And then, when I joined the opposition, it
was unthinkable that one day president Mugabe’s

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.600
government can be beaten.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.962
I lived to see Mugabe being beaten in 2008.

00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:11.300
I lived to see myself actually winning an
election as a member of parliament of course.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.440
But I also saw the brutal side of politics.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:22.070
Politics without rules is a recipe for disaster
for men and for mankind.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:27.380
There must be rules and they have necessarily
to be written.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:35.940
There must be social rules that govern people,
we can be this unfair but not that unfair.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:45.820
And what I have seen is that most politicians
go all the way to get what they want, inspective

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.380
of how they get it.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.780
So, in the world of politics, especially in
the world of politics, I have seen people

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.370
treat each other in the most despicable way
of manners.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:05.799
Mr. Mugabe, still president of your country,
was, if I remember correctly, one of those

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:16.900
freedom fighters to turn Rhodesia into Zimbabwe,
into a free African country.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.010
He became president, he is president for 36
years.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.950
What did you learn about the nature of power?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:32.154
I am asking you this because our first round
table conversation during the conference 'What

00:02:32.154 --> 00:02:37.070
will save the world?' will be about the defect
in society.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:42.080
Probably, the nature of power has something
to do with it.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.810
George Orwell, in 'Animal farm' was very prophetic.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:52.620
You would think that he wrote it with Zimbabwe
in mind.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:03:03.020
The way the animals fight, win together, get
power, and the way they treat each other when

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.890
the power is begotten.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.370
I think mr.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:15.660
Mugabe was a good fighter for liberation and
he did things well.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:23.270
Unfortunately, when we got into independence,
he founded the instruments of oppression used

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.930
by his predecessors.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:33.069
He could use them to suppress and he was tempted
to use these instruments.

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:40.569
So what that teaches us about the nature of
power is that you must limit it before a person

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:41.569
gets it.

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:54.890
The second thing is that a 
good leader in war time is not necessarily

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.410
a good leader in peace time.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:08.070
Unfortunately, the British had Churchill during
the war and I cannot think a better man motivating

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:15.020
his country to fight well, in a very difficult
war I suppose.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:21.249
To see that man at the end of that war losing
an election.

00:04:21.249 --> 00:04:28.550
I think it was the realization that you can
be good in war time but you are not necessarily

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:32.819
the best person to do the reconstruction of
the country.

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:36.080
I think Zimbabweans in Mugabe they forgot
that.

